   "h": "What happens next",
   "body": "<p>Psyche's troubles are far from over. She wanders in search of Cupid, while Venus, furious that her son has married a mortal she hates, hunts her down. Venus sets her a series of impossible tasks: sorting a vast heap of mixed grain in one night (the ants help her), fetching golden wool from savage sheep, bringing water from the source of the river Styx, and fetching a box of beauty from Proserpina in the underworld. On the way back Psyche opens the box out of curiosity and falls into a deathly sleep. Cupid, now healed, rescues her, and Jupiter makes her immortal so that the two can marry. Their daughter is called Voluptas, Pleasure.</p>"
